sn35.32:22.1 | S: The pleasant, painful, or neutral feeling that arises dependent on mind contact: is that permanent or impermanent?” | T: Is any feeling that arises with mind-contact as condition permanent or impermanent?”—
sn35.32:23.1 | S: “Impermanent, sir.” | T: “Impermanent, venerable sir.”—
sn35.32:24.1 | S: “But if it’s impermanent, is it suffering or happiness?” | T: “Is what is impermanent suffering or happiness?”—
sn35.32:25.1 | S: “Suffering, sir.” | T: “Suffering, venerable sir.”—
sn35.32:26.1 | S: “But if it’s impermanent, suffering, and perishable, is it fit to be regarded thus: | T: “Is what is impermanent, suffering, and subject to change fit to be regarded thus:
sn35.32:26.2 | S: ‘This is mine, I am this, this is my self’?” | T: ‘This is mine, this I am, this is my self’?”—
