sn35.32:28.1 | S: “Seeing this, a learned noble disciple grows disillusioned with the eye, sights, eye consciousness, and eye contact. | T: “Seeing thus, bhikkhus, the instructed noble disciple experiences revulsion towards the eye, towards forms, towards eye-consciousness, towards eye-contact,
sn35.32:28.2 | S: And they grow disillusioned with the painful, pleasant, or neutral feeling that arises dependent on eye contact. | T: towards whatever feeling arises with eye-contact as condition—whether pleasant or painful or neither-painful-nor-pleasant.
