## sn45.7
sn45.7:1.1 | S: At Sāvatthī. | T: (none)
sn45.7:1.2 | S: Then a mendicant went up to the Buddha … and said to him: | T: (none)
sn45.7:2.1 | S: “Sir, they speak of ‘the removal of greed, hate, and delusion’. | T: “Venerable sir, it is said, ‘the removal of lust, the removal of hatred, the removal of delusion.’
sn45.7:2.2 | S: What is this a term for?” | T: Of what now, venerable sir, is this the designation?”
sn45.7:2.3 | P: ‘rāgavinayo dosavinayo mohavinayo’”ti? | T: (none)
sn45.7:2.4 | S: “Mendicant, the removal of greed, hate, and delusion is a term for an element of extinguishment. | T: “This, bhikkhu, is a designation for the element of Nibbāna:
sn45.7:2.5 | P: ‘rāgavinayo dosavinayo mohavinayo’ti. | T: the removal of lust, the removal of hatred, the removal of delusion.
sn45.7:2.6 | S: It’s used to speak of the ending of defilements.” | T: The destruction of the taints is spoken of in that way.”
sn45.7:3.1 | S: When he said this, the mendicant said to the Buddha: | T: When this was said, that bhikkhu said to the Blessed One:
sn45.7:3.2 | S: “Sir, they speak of ‘freedom from death’. | T: “Venerable sir, it is said, ‘the Deathless, the Deathless.’
sn45.7:3.3 | S: What is freedom from death? And what is the path that leads to freedom from death?” | T: What now, venerable sir, is the Deathless? What is the path leading to the Deathless?”
sn45.7:3.4 | S: “The ending of greed, hate, and delusion. | T: “The destruction of lust, the destruction of hatred, the destruction of delusion:
sn45.7:3.5 | S: This is called freedom from death. | T: this is called the Deathless.
sn45.7:3.6 | S: The path that leads to freedom from death is simply this noble eightfold path, that is: | T: This Noble Eightfold Path is the path leading to the Deathless; that is,
sn45.7:3.7 | S: right view, right purpose, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness, and right immersion.” | T: right view … right concentration.”
sn45.7:3.8 | P: Sattamaṁ. | T: (none)


